## Request and progress evidence

request-evidence-report.md and request-evidence.json record runtime04's actual first and second investigator envelopes: 6,700 and 22,071 bytes, with prospective input bounds 10,305 and 27,370. Each has 16 evaluator headline items. These archived requests predate the current metric insertion and cannot demonstrate its dynamic execution.

Current source orders four headline metrics plus available integer counts from a closed 16-metric allowlist per episode, including zero values, then a rejection count if nonzero, then archive/history evidence. The four real parent episodes supply 64 available count values; this supports the possible 80-item zero-rejection projection together with static source inspection. Omission of a zero rejection count and the new request composition have no manufactured runtime coverage.

The archived request bounds fit actual06's stored capabilities individually. That analytical comparison is neither a future packet nor a fresh budget authorization. Its stored six-call/448,000-token capabilities and prior spend are historical facts. C-c must choose one coherent finite future call/token budget and exact initial packets before a new grant.

The lifecycle cap limits attempts. Rejected or failed attempts do not establish an evaluated feedback round. The required future success is two distinct actual evaluated rounds with critic, checkpoint and successful cleanup evidence.

